ON THE NUMBERS IN THIS PROJECT

Please read this before quoting anything from here.

Figures produced by the architecture model in perf_model/ are FIRST-ORDER
ESTIMATES, good to roughly a factor of two. They come from an analytical model,
not from synthesis, not from silicon, and not from measurement. Nothing has been
taped out or even synthesised. Seventeen modelling errors were found and
corrected during this work and most of them flattered the design, so treat any
figure that has not survived an adversarial read with suspicion — including the
ones here.

A smaller set of results IS measured, and is labelled as such in
PHASE0_FINDINGS.md and README.md: solver iteration counts from real OSQP,
numerical precision floors, and CPU timings on a stated host. Where a document
says MEASURED it means the numerics or the wall clock were actually observed on
the machine named; it does not mean silicon.

Efficiency figures elsewhere in the industry are frequently quoted without a
process node or a precision attached, which makes them uncomparable. This project
tries not to do that. If you find a figure here missing its node, precision, or
evidence class, that is a bug — please report it.

